{
	"name": "Hunter’s Snare",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/environment/traps/trap-jaw-steel.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 4th level, your hunter’s work with traps becomes effective in combat situations. With one minute of preparation, they can create the following traps once per short rest:</p><p><strong>Deadfall.</strong> By prepping a modestly sized tree or other tall, slender, object, the hunter can drop it when the time is right. As an action, they make a ranged weapon attack against a DC 15. On a successful hit, the tree falls and creates difficult terrain in a 15ft wide line 30ft long. You must choose the area when you build this trap.</p><p><strong>Snapvine.</strong> With a bent tree and a sturdy cord, the hunter yanks an opponent off their feet. When a creature enters the square that contains the snapvine trap, they make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, they are unable to move and are pulled up to 15ft in a direction chosen when this trap is created, and land [[/condition id=prone]].</p>",
